id: genetic-focus-arcosian
name: Genetic Focus: Arcosian
order: 3
category: body
# "[Uncanny Monster]": it replaces that Primary Racial Trait - which, the table's. (1) Its Prerequisite, the Arcosian Genes Factor Trait,
# shown and never enforced.
importance: primary
# (2) Read off the Trait itself, as Bio-Suit's: the Plating's Apparel Bonus is worked out before any effect has run (gear.mjs
# platingBonusPerTier).
platingBonusPerTier: 1
description: >
  Your Arcosian genes give you an overwhelmingly intimidating visage.
text: >
  Genetic Focus: Arcosian (Body) [Uncanny Monster]: Your Arcosian genes give you an overwhelmingly intimidating visage.
  (1)-[Prerequisite]: Arcosian Genes Factor Trait.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase the Apparel Bonus of your Plating by 1(T).
  (3)-[Passive]: Double the bonus to your Wound Rolls of your Tail Attack from your Adaptation Points.
  (4)-[Triggered]: If you spend Adaptation Points on the Wound Roll of an Attacking Maneuver, and a target of that Attacking Maneuver receives Damage, gain an Adaptation Point.
  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: If you knock an Opponent through a Health Threshold or Defeat them with an Attacking Maneuver, maximize your Adaptation Points. If you already had a number of Adaptation Points equal to or exceeding 1/2 of your maximum number of Adaptation Points, you may use the Energy Charge Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
---

[passive]
# (3) The Tail Attack's Wound Roll: the Adaptation Points spent on it 2(T) each (chat.mjs rollSide).
allow focusArcosian.tailWound;
# (5) An Opponent knocked through a Health Threshold, or Defeated, by your attack: always asked, once an Encounter - no Triggered/Automatic
# button, the use being the Encounter's one (the user's). Your Adaptation Points to their Maximum; had you half of it or more, the Energy
# Charge out of sequence, asked (combat.mjs, chat.mjs focusArcosianSurge).
allow focusArcosian.surge;

# (4) Adaptation Points spent on an attack's Wound Roll, and Damage worked out on a target of it - once an attack
# (adaptation-wound-damage). Automatic by default, its Triggered/Automatic button.
[triggered/adaptation-wound-damage, effect 4]
adaptation.stacks += 1;
